\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{45563d9}
\import{base-macros}

\p{A worker's overlay used to keep the size of the largest declaration of its session: the hash-consing index stayed at 16 MB on Init and at up to 256 MB per worker on Mathlib, so that every later probe was a cache miss. Cutting an overlay back to a mark now returns the node array to 32 MiB when what is kept fills at most a quarter of it, keeps the index proportional to the nodes it holds and releases the literals made since the mark; the literal pool retires released indices instead of reusing them. The builder frees its loader state when the load ends (288 MiB on Mathlib), and the store reports its memory by region. Published with 67 tests green after a gate with the reference engine and one worker: 230 of 230 tests correct, and 0 soundness and 0 completeness differences on 12,260 tutorial mutants (11,847 agree, 413 declined) and on 2,692 mutants of the bugs corpus (2,627 agree, 65 declined).}

\p{Detail: \src{rlvm-store/README.md}. Commit \commit{45563d9}. Session: [foundation modules and the reference pipeline](ses-BQZM).}
